1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,769
听：A Misunderstanding.

2
00:00:01,769 --> 00:00:03,537
跟读：A Misunderstanding.

3
00:00:03,537 --> 00:00:29,438
听：In general, spoken statements are the major way of communication, but body language and facial expressions also have such kinds of function. For example, yawning means not being interested and turning one’s back to someone or swinging your fist shows your anger. But what those gestures really mean is subjective in different cultures.

4
00:00:29,438 --> 00:00:55,338
跟读：In general, spoken statements are the major way of communication, but body language and facial expressions also have such kinds of function. For example, yawning means not being interested and turning one’s back to someone or swinging your fist shows your anger. But what those gestures really mean is subjective in different cultures.

5
00:00:55,338 --> 00:01:21,297
听：Thus, misunderstandings happen now and then in today’s world of cultural crossroads. Once, representing the Adults’ Education Association, I went to the airport to meet an official of high rank from Colombia and take him to his dormitory and then to the canteen. After the flight arrived, I saw a man looking around curiously.

6
00:01:21,297 --> 00:01:47,256
跟读：Thus, misunderstandings happen now and then in today’s world of cultural crossroads. Once, representing the Adults’ Education Association, I went to the airport to meet an official of high rank from Colombia and take him to his dormitory and then to the canteen. After the flight arrived, I saw a man looking around curiously.

7
00:01:47,256 --> 00:02:01,435
听：So I approached to greet him. He suddenly dashed to hug me and kissed me on both cheeks. As a young girl, I felt truly embarrassed and put up my hands to defend myself.

8
00:02:01,435 --> 00:02:15,613
跟读：So I approached to greet him. He suddenly dashed to hug me and kissed me on both cheeks. As a young girl, I felt truly embarrassed and put up my hands to defend myself.

9
00:02:15,613 --> 00:02:32,337
听：His false smile told me that he had lost face. Later, I received a cassette from him, in which he recorded his apology. On hearing that Colombians were more likely to kiss others, I soon felt at ease.

10
00:02:32,337 --> 00:02:49,060
跟读：His false smile told me that he had lost face. Later, I received a cassette from him, in which he recorded his apology. On hearing that Colombians were more likely to kiss others, I soon felt at ease.
